00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:03.900
Now, what you're seeing right now

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:07.110
is the Fed's senior loan
officer opinion survey

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:09.060
and this just is basically
the percentage of

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:11.340
banks that say they're tightening
their lending standards.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.650
What that means is they're
making it harder to give

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:15.720
out loans requiring more from people.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:18.330
Maybe it's higher credit scores,
maybe it's more collateral.

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:20.820
Basically just saying we're
making it a bit tougher

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:23.130
because we're worried
about lending money out.

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:25.380
Now that number you see there
at the edge of your screen,

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:28.290
the latest number where
we are, that's about 45%

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:30.390
of banks saying they are
tightening lending standards,

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:32.370
making it harder to give out loans.

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:36.300
We are already in the area
which typically historically,

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.440
if you look on your screen there

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:40.470
you see all those little shaded
areas that note recession.

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:43.350
Every time we get to the level
that we are at right now,

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:45.270
level that we were at in January,

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:46.620
this isn't even where we are right now.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.260
This is before this banking crisis issue.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:50.310
We have had a recession.

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:53.670
So that's why this survey
is very informative.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:55.650
It tells you about
historical trends we have

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:58.380
seen going back all the way 30 years.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:00.660
The study started in the
1990s and as you see,

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:02.730
when we get to the levels
that we're at right now,

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:05.520
there has been a recession
every single time.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:07.320
So wanted to just put
that on your screen to

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:10.080
illustrate the historical
trend of this survey

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:13.650
and why it's been a fairly
accurate predictor of recessions.

