00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:51.645
and Global Services PMI,
that's Wednesday and Thursday.

00:03:51.645 --> 00:03:54.600
PMI surveys, Purchasing Managers Indexes,

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.700
basically are where these companies go out

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:58.657
and they say to businesses,
"Hey, how are you doing?

00:03:58.657 --> 00:04:00.217
"Are you ordering more?
Are you ordering less?

00:04:00.217 --> 00:04:01.987
"Are you hiring more, hiring less?

00:04:01.987 --> 00:04:03.900
"Are things costing more, costing less?"

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:06.210
And then they put together
a sentiment index.

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:08.580
50, anything above 50 mean
things are going well,

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:10.500
they're improving, anything below 50

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:11.760
means they're getting worse.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:13.560
We will get a bunch of
those out this week.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.510
And in fact we just got one this morning,

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:17.010
